WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.061
India's rain comes with the monsoon.

2
00:00:03.643 --> 00:00:05.241
So why does Delhi get rain

3
00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:05.855
in winter?

4
00:00:06.091 --> 00:00:08.412
Blame a storm from the Mediterranean.

5
00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:10.411
A western disturbance is

6
00:00:10.411 --> 00:00:11.955
an extratropical storm,

7
00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:14.504
born over the Mediterranean

8
00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:15.635
or Caspian Sea.

9
00:00:16.271 --> 00:00:18.307
The westerlies carry it east,

10
00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:20.969
across Iran, Afghanistan

11
00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:22.187
and Pakistan,

12
00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:23.443
into India.

13
00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.093
When it meets the Himalayas,

14
00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.199
it brings rain to the plains

15
00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:28.966
and heavy snow to the hills.

16
00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:30.959
That winter rain matters

17
00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:31.932
for rabi crops.

18
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:33.474
Too much can damage them,

19
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.761
and bring landslides and

20
00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:36.545
avalanches.

21
00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:38.521
The monsoon is tropical,

22
00:00:38.521 --> 00:00:40.610
and carries its moisture low.

23
00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:42.754
A western disturbance carries

24
00:00:42.754 --> 00:00:43.469
it higher up.

25
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:44.626
Different storm.

26
00:00:44.951 --> 00:00:45.753
Different season.

27
00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:46.585
Your turn.

28
00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.445
Where do western disturbances

29
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:48.968
come from?
